1
00:02:30,039 --> 00:02:35,439
This is the time known as the Great Pirate Era.

2
00:02:35,739 --> 00:02:39,739
A countless array of pirates go to battle across the seas in search of the One Piece,

3
00:02:39,999 --> 00:02:43,939
the legendary treasure left behind by Gold Roger, King of the Pirates.

4
00:02:44,539 --> 00:02:48,819
Bucky D. Luffy, a boy whose body turned to rubber after eating the gum gum fruit,

5
00:02:49,099 --> 00:02:51,579
set sail to become the next King of the Pirates.

6
00:02:51,959 --> 00:02:54,539
As Luffy and his crew conquer numerous obstacles,

7
00:02:54,859 --> 00:02:57,679
they capture the unwanted attention of the world government,

8
00:02:57,679 --> 00:03:00,719
which will use any means necessary to stop them.

9
00:03:02,539 --> 00:03:03,979
This is sight!

10
00:03:04,719 --> 00:03:07,519
Can't wait to see what kind of adventure's up next!

11
00:03:08,039 --> 00:03:11,059
With a charted course awash in danger and intrigue,

12
00:03:11,279 --> 00:03:15,339
the crew will cut a path across the Grand Line to the New World.

13
00:03:19,179 --> 00:03:22,179
Separated from his crew, Luffy and his newfound cohorts

14
00:03:22,179 --> 00:03:25,379
have hijacked a Navy ship in order to rescue his brother Ace,

15
00:03:25,379 --> 00:03:28,519
who's been transported to Navy HQ for execution.

16
00:03:29,819 --> 00:03:32,279
You've been condemned in your sentences final.

17
00:03:32,679 --> 00:03:36,159
There is not but despair on the path before you, however you may struggle.

18
00:03:36,679 --> 00:03:38,539
Can't you see you're wasting your time?

19
00:03:38,799 --> 00:03:40,399
All filthy criminals such as you,

20
00:03:40,519 --> 00:03:42,459
the gates of justice will never open!

21
00:03:42,459 --> 00:03:48,699
You're sure you want to open the gates of justice at a time like this?

22
00:03:49,819 --> 00:03:51,599
All this time and you knew!

23
00:03:52,139 --> 00:03:53,619
I got you!

24
00:03:55,079 --> 00:03:56,479
You silly man!

25
00:03:56,939 --> 00:03:57,719
Come on!

26
00:03:58,079 --> 00:03:59,399
Answer me!

27
00:04:01,099 --> 00:04:02,259
This is it!

28
00:04:02,859 --> 00:04:04,579
The gate's about to close!

29
00:04:04,999 --> 00:04:05,459
We have...

30
00:04:06,459 --> 00:04:07,459
to go!

31
00:04:07,459 --> 00:04:11,259
To make you!

32
00:04:12,039 --> 00:04:13,279
The gate is closing!

33
00:04:13,539 --> 00:04:14,519
Keep firing!

34
00:04:14,879 --> 00:04:15,779
Take them out!

35
00:04:16,039 --> 00:04:18,459
Any last words before I eliminate you?

36
00:04:18,699 --> 00:04:19,719
Have at me!

37
00:04:21,819 --> 00:04:26,019
Luffy has successfully broken out of the world's most impenetrable prison,

38
00:04:26,299 --> 00:04:27,019
Impel Down.

39
00:04:27,819 --> 00:04:31,819
Although, the end of this battle is nowhere in sight.

40
00:04:31,819 --> 00:04:37,839
To the Navy headquarters!

41
00:04:37,839 --> 00:04:39,499
Off to rescue Ace!

42
00:04:49,239 --> 00:04:51,419
Living dangerously is one thing,

43
00:04:51,679 --> 00:04:53,019
living carelessly another.

44
00:04:53,599 --> 00:04:56,039
If I'd lack the foresight to bring an antidote,

45
00:04:56,299 --> 00:04:58,639
I'd be stumbling over your corpses right now.

46
00:04:59,059 --> 00:05:01,259
Don't ever underestimate Magellan.

47
00:05:01,819 --> 00:05:03,619
Ha ha ha ha!

48
00:05:03,619 --> 00:05:05,119
But we're here!

49
00:05:05,599 --> 00:05:07,339
You shouldn't dismiss your own inclusion.

50
00:05:08,119 --> 00:05:10,479
Your presence is a factor in our fate as well.

51
00:05:12,539 --> 00:05:14,059
Though, he's right.

52
00:05:14,259 --> 00:05:15,759
I was sure I was a dead man.

53
00:05:16,339 --> 00:05:17,839
We're lucky we're all...

54
00:05:17,839 --> 00:05:19,839
still alive.

55
00:05:25,519 --> 00:05:28,239
Well, it ain't up to us whether we'll ever die.

56
00:05:28,459 --> 00:05:30,519
Fear of death is the fastest way to lose.

57
00:05:31,819 --> 00:05:33,619
See, ha ha ha!

58
00:05:33,619 --> 00:05:34,899
Just live what you can,

59
00:05:35,119 --> 00:05:36,419
even if it kills you.

60
00:05:37,519 --> 00:05:37,959
Right?

61
00:05:38,219 --> 00:05:39,199
See, ha ha ha ha!

62
00:05:39,199 --> 00:05:49,899
Still, don't think I ain't grateful for your help.

63
00:05:49,899 --> 00:05:53,859
Still, don't think I ain't grateful for your help.

64
00:05:54,259 --> 00:05:55,019
Because I am.

65
00:05:55,559 --> 00:05:57,359
And again, welcome to our gang.

66
00:05:57,819 --> 00:05:59,599
I bet we'll make a great team.

67
00:05:59,599 --> 00:06:02,739
I don't see much future for myself in this crit.

68
00:06:03,179 --> 00:06:06,679
You're exactly the sort of person I've wanted to meet for some time.

69
00:06:06,679 --> 00:06:08,479
See, ha ha ha ha ha!

70
00:06:08,479 --> 00:06:08,979
See, ha ha ha ha!

71
00:06:08,979 --> 00:06:09,479
See, ha ha ha ha!

72
00:06:09,479 --> 00:06:10,479
See, ha ha ha ha!

73
00:06:10,479 --> 00:06:12,479
See, ha ha ha ha!

74
00:06:12,479 --> 00:06:13,479
See, ha ha ha ha!

75
00:06:20,479 --> 00:06:21,479
Gather round, men.

76
00:06:21,479 --> 00:06:22,479
The time has come.

77
00:06:22,479 --> 00:06:26,479
Let's raise a toast to our unprecedented escape from Impel Down!

78
00:06:26,479 --> 00:06:27,479
To us!

79
00:06:27,479 --> 00:06:28,479
To us!

80
00:06:28,479 --> 00:06:29,479
To us!

81
00:06:29,479 --> 00:06:30,479
To us!

82
00:06:30,479 --> 00:06:31,479
To us!

83
00:06:31,479 --> 00:06:32,479
To us!

84
00:06:42,479 --> 00:06:43,479
Damn, what is that?

85
00:06:43,479 --> 00:06:54,239
I'm afraid we'll have to do without Inazuma from here.

86
00:06:54,439 --> 00:06:57,539
Wait, are you trying to tell us the infection is that serious?

87
00:06:57,979 --> 00:07:01,479
I was lucky that Magellan hit me with only one type of poison.

88
00:07:01,979 --> 00:07:06,559
I was able to flush it out of my system using my healing and energy hormones.

89
00:07:08,459 --> 00:07:09,699
Hee-haw!

90
00:07:10,639 --> 00:07:12,519
It's an ambivalent fix, though.

91
00:07:12,519 --> 00:07:16,999
One hormone will take years off my life, while the other causes severe side effects.

92
00:07:17,599 --> 00:07:22,479
So for him, the best thing possible is good old-fashioned bed rest and natural rehabilitation.

93
00:07:23,439 --> 00:07:30,659
Nothing can help you to regain the years lost by using the hormone Inazuma is an indispensable newcomer of the Revolutionary Army.

94
00:07:31,239 --> 00:07:34,999
We need him healthy, so we have to make sure he recovers slow and easy.

95
00:07:42,519 --> 00:07:47,599
Now that I think about it, he wasn't such a pain in the butt after all.

96
00:07:47,599 --> 00:07:53,659
He was such a good guy, and he got God-saving us.

97
00:07:53,659 --> 00:07:59,779
Brother Bon!

98
00:07:59,879 --> 00:08:00,799
Brother Bon!

99
00:08:00,879 --> 00:08:01,879
Brother Bon!

100
00:08:02,179 --> 00:08:03,619
Brother Bon!

101
00:08:03,619 --> 00:08:15,899
Hey, come on, guys.

102
00:08:15,959 --> 00:08:18,739
It's sad and all, but you can't waste your whole life's mourning.

103
00:08:19,179 --> 00:08:22,099
He was great, but now he's dead, and that's the way it is.

104
00:08:22,099 --> 00:08:24,719
So all he can do is party.

105
00:08:25,599 --> 00:08:26,899
That's what he would want.

106
00:08:29,899 --> 00:08:31,019
So there you go.

107
00:08:31,099 --> 00:08:33,439
It can double as a funeral for Mr. Two.

108
00:08:33,439 --> 00:08:34,659
Oh, Christ!

109
00:08:34,659 --> 00:08:46,159
Hey, for all we know, there's still a chance Bon didn't even get killed, you big nose.

110
00:08:46,279 --> 00:08:48,079
Oh, hey, what did you just say to me?

111
00:08:48,259 --> 00:08:51,859
You've got a big, stupid nose to go along with your big, stupid face.

112
00:08:51,919 --> 00:08:55,039
Oh, how about I stretch your stupid face until it's...

113
00:08:55,039 --> 00:08:57,459
Oh, blew it out your giant nose.

114
00:08:57,739 --> 00:09:00,339
If you ask me, they both look like idiots.

115
00:09:00,339 --> 00:09:09,179
Fancy trick how you rallied those sharks.

116
00:09:09,679 --> 00:09:10,559
How'd you do it?

117
00:09:10,639 --> 00:09:14,259
I was under the impression only mermaids have the ability to speak to fish.

118
00:09:14,599 --> 00:09:16,799
But that impression is clearly incorrect.

119
00:09:18,019 --> 00:09:18,859
Is that odd?

120
00:09:19,059 --> 00:09:21,559
A fish man being friends with fish?

121
00:09:22,279 --> 00:09:24,839
Well, it's not the usual, I know that.

122
00:09:25,199 --> 00:09:26,519
You're a strange one, huh?

123
00:09:26,519 --> 00:09:30,279
A misfit of the savage species.

124
00:09:30,899 --> 00:09:33,559
Fine, I'll take that as a compliment of sorts.

125
00:09:34,739 --> 00:09:35,819
Yes, it's true.

126
00:09:36,039 --> 00:09:37,799
Fishmen do have a violent nature.

127
00:09:38,239 --> 00:09:39,899
Bon is not dead, damn it!

128
00:09:41,479 --> 00:09:41,999
Whoa!

129
00:09:42,459 --> 00:09:44,799
Captain Buggy threw another big red nose!

130
00:09:47,599 --> 00:09:48,059
Luffy.

131
00:09:48,819 --> 00:09:49,139
Huh?

132
00:09:49,139 --> 00:09:51,879
I wouldn't be here if it weren't for you.

133
00:09:52,399 --> 00:09:54,479
You gave me the chance to rescue Ace.

134
00:09:55,179 --> 00:09:57,479
And I owe you a great debt.

135
00:09:57,979 --> 00:09:59,319
Don't think about it like that.

136
00:09:59,599 --> 00:10:00,159
We're even.

137
00:10:01,239 --> 00:10:03,279
And besides, you're super strong.

138
00:10:03,519 --> 00:10:05,419
I'm just happy to have you on the team.

139
00:10:06,199 --> 00:10:07,939
I wish I could thank him properly.

140
00:10:08,379 --> 00:10:11,939
And apologize for my involvement in that unfortunate situation.

141
00:10:12,899 --> 00:10:15,139
But no, this isn't the time.

142
00:10:15,919 --> 00:10:17,859
We have enough to worry about for now.

143
00:10:17,859 --> 00:10:21,879
I only hope my strength will be enough.

144
00:10:22,319 --> 00:10:24,399
I may be one of the seven warlords,

145
00:10:24,559 --> 00:10:26,719
but they'll strip me of my title after this.

146
00:10:27,039 --> 00:10:30,599
Now let's make Navy Headquarters regret the ever laid hands on Ace.

147
00:10:31,419 --> 00:10:33,579
We must do right by our fallen.

148
00:10:34,359 --> 00:10:37,339
We'll make your friend proud and rescue Ace at any cost.

149
00:10:38,659 --> 00:10:40,799
Warlord Navy Headquarters?

150
00:10:41,719 --> 00:10:42,219
What?

151
00:10:43,819 --> 00:10:44,859
Oh, really?

152
00:10:44,859 --> 00:10:47,459
You're seriously a warlord?

153
00:10:47,639 --> 00:10:49,619
Geez, no wonder you're so strong.

154
00:10:52,679 --> 00:10:53,239
Yes.

155
00:10:53,459 --> 00:10:55,299
I suppose I should have told you sooner.

156
00:10:55,539 --> 00:10:57,339
Everybody else knew that.

157
00:10:57,619 --> 00:10:58,099
Hey!

158
00:10:58,559 --> 00:11:00,799
What's all this talk about Navy Headquarters?

159
00:11:01,159 --> 00:11:03,179
Don't tell me we escaped from the bowels of hell

160
00:11:03,179 --> 00:11:05,319
just to head straight back into the jaws of the beast!

161
00:11:05,319 --> 00:11:07,259
I'm afraid so.

162
00:11:07,379 --> 00:11:08,159
Screw you!

163
00:11:08,439 --> 00:11:09,679
Nobody is that crazy!

164
00:11:09,979 --> 00:11:13,279
Surely you guys heard about the war brewing between Whitebeard and the Navy!

165
00:11:14,099 --> 00:11:14,919
Uh, war?

166
00:11:15,159 --> 00:11:16,139
Navy Headquarters.

167
00:11:16,599 --> 00:11:18,299
Don't act like it's a big surprise.

168
00:11:18,959 --> 00:11:20,719
Not our fault you're so dense.

169
00:11:20,919 --> 00:11:21,319
Say what?!

170
00:11:21,319 --> 00:11:23,799
Well, we passed through the Gate of Justice.

171
00:11:24,119 --> 00:11:24,859
Isn't that right?

172
00:11:25,099 --> 00:11:28,099
Our destination is Eni's Lobby or Navy HQ.

173
00:11:28,839 --> 00:11:31,739
This tub current is restricted to government passage only.

174
00:11:32,159 --> 00:11:35,619
It's one giant whirlpool that connects the government's three major facilities.

175
00:11:36,419 --> 00:11:39,799
The reason we bust it out now is because we have a role to play in this war.

176
00:11:40,219 --> 00:11:41,639
So you best get used to it.

177
00:11:41,639 --> 00:11:45,839
Yeah, the real fight's about to start.

178
00:11:46,479 --> 00:11:47,239
Real fight?

179
00:11:47,359 --> 00:11:49,059
Then what you call it back there!

180
00:11:49,259 --> 00:11:49,819
No way!

181
00:11:50,079 --> 00:11:51,719
No way to tell us about this!

182
00:11:52,059 --> 00:11:52,559
Stop!

183
00:11:52,699 --> 00:11:54,359
Turn this ship around, you bastard!

184
00:11:54,599 --> 00:11:55,019
Freeze!

185
00:11:55,139 --> 00:11:55,539
Stop!

186
00:11:55,699 --> 00:11:57,779
There's no stopping and there's no turning around.

187
00:11:57,979 --> 00:11:59,419
Not while the ship's on the current.

188
00:11:59,779 --> 00:12:01,639
If you're scared, just get off.

189
00:12:02,219 --> 00:12:07,359
We can't do that, moron!

190
00:12:07,499 --> 00:12:08,599
That would kill us!

191
00:12:08,799 --> 00:12:10,319
We both have devil fruit power!

192
00:12:10,319 --> 00:12:11,059
Navy HQ!

193
00:12:11,059 --> 00:12:15,579
You, the warlords, and the white-beard pirates all fighting each other at once!

194
00:12:15,819 --> 00:12:17,419
Nobody can survive that!

195
00:12:34,459 --> 00:12:35,439
I've heard enough.

196
00:12:35,619 --> 00:12:36,499
Please take me back.

197
00:12:36,499 --> 00:12:38,799
I'd rather be in prison than this war.

198
00:12:38,799 --> 00:12:42,539
All of us from New Common Land knew about this plan.

199
00:12:42,739 --> 00:12:45,319
Then why the hell didn't you tell us?!

200
00:12:45,319 --> 00:12:49,899
This is it!

201
00:12:49,999 --> 00:12:50,819
We're all dead!

202
00:12:51,199 --> 00:12:51,639
Mommy!

203
00:12:51,639 --> 00:12:52,139
Hey!

204
00:12:52,139 --> 00:13:04,059
What is that?

205
00:13:04,319 --> 00:13:05,279
You guys hear it?

206
00:13:05,279 --> 00:13:19,839
It's a transponder snail.

207
00:13:19,839 --> 00:13:23,839
It's a transponder snail.

208
00:13:23,839 --> 00:13:24,839
But who's calling?

209
00:13:24,839 --> 00:13:25,839
But who's calling?

210
00:13:25,839 --> 00:13:26,839
Don't you get it?

211
00:13:26,839 --> 00:13:27,839
Think!

212
00:13:27,839 --> 00:13:28,839
We're on a Navy ship!

213
00:13:28,839 --> 00:13:29,839
Huh?

214
00:13:29,839 --> 00:13:30,339
Well...

215
00:13:30,339 --> 00:13:30,839
What's this?

216
00:13:30,839 --> 00:13:31,939
How was this?

217
00:13:31,939 --> 00:13:32,399
It's a tapetang!

218
00:13:32,559 --> 00:13:33,339
It's a Saiyan ship's army ship!

219
00:13:34,439 --> 00:13:59,199
Scottie's Phi-

220
00:13:59,199 --> 00:14:28,979
It's just that I know what's here.

221
00:14:29,199 --> 00:14:33,199
Uh, hello?

222
00:14:33,199 --> 00:14:35,199
He answered it!

223
00:14:35,199 --> 00:14:37,199
Greetings, from Navy HQ.

224
00:14:37,199 --> 00:14:38,199
Hey, Luffy here.

225
00:14:38,199 --> 00:14:40,199
Idiot, don't say that!

226
00:14:40,199 --> 00:14:44,199
Listen, kid, we're aware that the ship has been hijacked by escabies.

227
00:14:44,199 --> 00:14:48,199
We received a report from Impel Down, so let's be honest here.

228
00:14:48,199 --> 00:14:53,199
Before contact was lost, we had insider information being fed to us.

229
00:14:53,199 --> 00:14:57,199
Based on this, we've determined who the two ringleaders behind the breakout are.

230
00:14:57,199 --> 00:14:58,199
Two?

231
00:14:58,199 --> 00:15:05,199
You, the pirate known as Straw Hat Luffy, and another notorious pirate, Buggy the Clown.

232
00:15:05,199 --> 00:15:07,199
Eh?

233
00:15:07,199 --> 00:15:08,199
Whoa!

234
00:15:08,199 --> 00:15:09,199
Wait, what?

235
00:15:09,199 --> 00:15:10,199
Ringleader?

236
00:15:10,199 --> 00:15:11,199
Seriously?

237
00:15:11,199 --> 00:15:14,199
We've got warlords here, and their main suspect is Captain Buggy?

238
00:15:14,199 --> 00:15:15,199
Who the hell are you?

239
00:15:15,199 --> 00:15:17,199
Come clean with us!

240
00:15:17,199 --> 00:15:18,199
No!

241
00:15:18,199 --> 00:15:19,199
Why me?

242
00:15:19,199 --> 00:15:21,199
Pass me the documents.

243
00:15:21,199 --> 00:15:22,199
Here.

244
00:15:22,199 --> 00:15:23,199
Thank you.

245
00:15:23,199 --> 00:15:26,199
At first, we just assumed that the clown was another two-bit criminal.

246
00:15:26,199 --> 00:15:30,199
But to be frank, we were wrong.

247
00:15:30,199 --> 00:15:34,199
We learned he was a crew member on the ship of Gold Roger, King of the Pirates.

248
00:15:34,199 --> 00:15:35,199
Ah!

249
00:15:35,199 --> 00:15:36,199
They found me out!

250
00:15:36,199 --> 00:15:37,199
What?

251
00:15:37,199 --> 00:15:38,199
What?

252
00:15:38,199 --> 00:15:40,199
You crewed on the Oro Jackson?

253
00:15:40,199 --> 00:15:41,199
Unbelievable!

254
00:15:41,199 --> 00:15:42,199
You're a star!

255
00:15:42,199 --> 00:15:44,199
A star among pirates!

256
00:15:44,199 --> 00:15:45,199
Oh, and there's one other thing.

257
00:15:45,199 --> 00:15:48,199
He's an ally of one of the four emperors.

258
00:15:48,199 --> 00:15:50,199
His name is Red-Haired Shanks.

259
00:15:50,199 --> 00:15:51,199
Are you serious?!

260
00:15:51,199 --> 00:15:54,199
So, if you can hear us, Buggy.

261
00:15:54,199 --> 00:15:58,199
We don't know how someone with your background has laid low for so long.

262
00:15:58,199 --> 00:16:01,199
But you most certainly stepped into the spotlight now.

263
00:16:01,199 --> 00:16:04,199
Well...

264
00:16:04,199 --> 00:16:07,199
We haven't defined your connection with Firefist Ace yet.

265
00:16:07,199 --> 00:16:10,199
But we're sure you share the same goal with Straw Hat Luffy.

266
00:16:10,199 --> 00:16:12,199
To rescue him from execution.

267
00:16:12,199 --> 00:16:15,199
Not really.

268
00:16:15,199 --> 00:16:20,199
We know that you're accompanied by Jinbei, Crocodile, Ivanka.

269
00:16:20,199 --> 00:16:26,199
Not to mention the more than 200 average run-of-the-mill ruffians you tricked into following your lead.

270
00:16:26,199 --> 00:16:28,199
Now let me explain your future.

271
00:16:28,199 --> 00:16:31,199
Your fates depend on whether we open the gate of justice.

272
00:16:31,199 --> 00:16:35,199
As long as we leave it closed, you can't get to Marine Four.

273
00:16:35,199 --> 00:16:37,199
And you can't even get out of the tub current.

274
00:16:37,199 --> 00:16:39,199
You will be completely stranded.

275
00:16:39,199 --> 00:16:42,199
There is no sea for you to escape to.

276
00:16:44,199 --> 00:16:46,199
Better get used to your surroundings.

277
00:16:46,199 --> 00:16:47,199
That's all.

278
00:16:47,199 --> 00:16:48,199
Hey!

279
00:16:48,199 --> 00:16:49,199
Wait!

280
00:16:49,199 --> 00:16:50,199
Navy!

281
00:16:50,199 --> 00:16:54,199
I'm gonna rescue Ace no matter what!

282
00:16:56,199 --> 00:16:58,199
Better keep your potatoes peeled!

283
00:16:59,199 --> 00:17:00,199
Or what?

284
00:17:06,199 --> 00:17:07,199
What?

285
00:17:07,199 --> 00:17:08,199
The things keep your eyes peeled!

286
00:17:08,199 --> 00:17:10,199
Now I'm gonna be craving potatoes!

287
00:17:10,199 --> 00:17:11,199
Thanks a lot, pal!

288
00:17:11,199 --> 00:17:15,199
He just tried to pick a fight with Navy HQ.

289
00:17:15,199 --> 00:17:16,199
Forget the potatoes!

290
00:17:16,199 --> 00:17:17,199
Wait!

291
00:17:17,199 --> 00:17:18,199
I've gotta know, Captain Buggy!

292
00:17:18,199 --> 00:17:22,199
Were you honestly a member of Gold Raunch's crew?

293
00:17:22,199 --> 00:17:24,199
And a sworn brother of red-haired Shanks?

294
00:17:24,199 --> 00:17:28,199
You should've said you're one hell of a pirate, Captain Buggy!

295
00:17:28,199 --> 00:17:30,199
Now, hold on!

296
00:17:30,199 --> 00:17:31,199
Aw, dammit!

297
00:17:31,199 --> 00:17:35,199
The government's never gonna let me out of their sights now that the truth's out!

298
00:17:35,199 --> 00:17:36,199
Not the background I was expecting from him!

299
00:17:36,199 --> 00:17:38,199
Not the background I was expecting from him!

300
00:17:38,199 --> 00:17:41,199
And yet he's so weak!

301
00:17:41,199 --> 00:17:42,199
That pedigree?

302
00:17:42,199 --> 00:17:43,199
That pedigree?

303
00:17:43,199 --> 00:17:44,199
And he's so petty?

304
00:17:44,199 --> 00:17:46,199
Every ship has one.

305
00:17:46,199 --> 00:17:48,199
A little blemish, I mean.

306
00:17:48,199 --> 00:17:51,199
Shut your mouth!

307
00:17:51,199 --> 00:17:54,199
You know, actually...

308
00:17:54,199 --> 00:17:59,199
Perhaps you've heard of a pirate named Buggy from the East Blue.

309
00:17:59,199 --> 00:18:02,199
The old vice-captain guy said something about you.

310
00:18:02,199 --> 00:18:03,199
Huh?

311
00:18:03,199 --> 00:18:04,199
The vice-captain?

312
00:18:04,199 --> 00:18:07,199
Yeah, the old guy, Rayleigh.

313
00:18:07,199 --> 00:18:08,199
You know him, right?

314
00:18:08,199 --> 00:18:09,199
Do I?

315
00:18:09,199 --> 00:18:12,199
Are you saying that you've actually seen Rayleigh?

316
00:18:12,199 --> 00:18:13,199
Aw, man!

317
00:18:13,199 --> 00:18:14,199
I miss that guy!

318
00:18:14,199 --> 00:18:15,199
Where'd you see him?

319
00:18:15,199 --> 00:18:18,199
They're talking about Dark King Rayleigh!

320
00:18:18,199 --> 00:18:19,199
Like it's no big deal!

321
00:18:19,199 --> 00:18:20,199
Huh?

322
00:18:20,199 --> 00:18:22,199
Holy crap, Captain Buggy!

323
00:18:22,199 --> 00:18:25,199
I knew you were the genuine article!

324
00:18:25,199 --> 00:18:26,199
No!

325
00:18:26,199 --> 00:18:27,199
Look, not so fast!

326
00:18:27,199 --> 00:18:32,199
Everything is true, yes, but you can't go spreading this around willy-nilly.

327
00:18:32,199 --> 00:18:34,199
We gotta think about my future as a pirate!

328
00:18:34,199 --> 00:18:35,199
Wow!

329
00:18:35,199 --> 00:18:38,199
I can't believe you're a member of such a legendary crew!

330
00:18:38,199 --> 00:18:39,199
Buggy!

331
00:18:39,199 --> 00:18:40,199
Buggy!

332
00:18:40,199 --> 00:18:41,199
Buggy!

333
00:18:41,199 --> 00:18:42,199
Buggy!

334
00:18:42,199 --> 00:18:43,199
Buggy!

335
00:18:43,199 --> 00:18:44,199
Buggy!

336
00:18:44,199 --> 00:18:45,199
Buggy!

337
00:18:45,199 --> 00:18:46,199
Shut up already!

338
00:18:46,199 --> 00:18:47,199
I was an apprentice, that's all!

339
00:18:47,199 --> 00:18:48,199
Buggy!

340
00:18:48,199 --> 00:18:49,199
Buggy!

341
00:18:49,199 --> 00:18:50,199
Buggy!

342
00:18:50,199 --> 00:18:51,199
Buggy!

343
00:18:51,199 --> 00:18:54,199
You can't worship me for that!

344
00:18:54,199 --> 00:18:55,199
Buggy!

345
00:18:55,199 --> 00:18:56,199
Buggy!

346
00:18:56,199 --> 00:18:57,199
Buggy!

347
00:18:57,199 --> 00:18:58,199
Buggy!

348
00:18:58,199 --> 00:18:59,199
Buggy!

349
00:18:59,199 --> 00:19:00,199
Buggy!

350
00:19:00,199 --> 00:19:01,199
Buggy!

351
00:19:01,199 --> 00:19:02,199
Buggy!

352
00:19:02,199 --> 00:19:03,199
Buggy!

353
00:19:03,199 --> 00:19:04,199
Buggy!

354
00:19:04,199 --> 00:19:05,199
Buggy!

355
00:19:05,199 --> 00:19:06,199
Buggy!

356
00:19:06,199 --> 00:19:07,199
Buggy!

357
00:19:07,199 --> 00:19:08,199
Buggy!

358
00:19:08,199 --> 00:19:09,199
Buggy!

359
00:19:09,199 --> 00:19:10,199
Buggy!

360
00:19:10,199 --> 00:19:11,199
Buggy!

361
00:19:11,199 --> 00:19:12,199
Buggy!

362
00:19:12,199 --> 00:19:13,199
Buggy!

363
00:19:13,199 --> 00:19:14,199
Buggy!

364
00:19:14,199 --> 00:19:16,199
Only there was some way.

365
00:19:18,199 --> 00:19:19,699
If I could defeat Whitebeard,

366
00:19:19,699 --> 00:19:22,699
maybe I could become one of the four emperors.

367
00:19:22,699 --> 00:19:24,199
Hell yes!

368
00:19:24,199 --> 00:19:25,699
Wait, no, no, no, no, no, no.

369
00:19:25,699 --> 00:19:29,699
I would need to become the King of the Pirates!

370
00:19:30,699 --> 00:19:31,699
It's perfect.

371
00:19:31,699 --> 00:19:34,199
Some of these guys have probably got higher bounties

372
00:19:34,199 --> 00:19:35,699
on their heads than I do.

373
00:19:35,699 --> 00:19:37,699
If I play my cards just right...

374
00:19:40,699 --> 00:19:42,699
I can do this!

375
00:19:42,699 --> 00:19:46,699
Captain Buggy, we'll follow you until the day we die!

376
00:19:48,699 --> 00:19:50,199
Just give us an order!

377
00:19:50,199 --> 00:19:52,199
Like steal this ship from the guys who stole it!

378
00:19:52,199 --> 00:19:53,699
We don't have to go to Navy HQ!

379
00:19:53,699 --> 00:19:56,699
That's right, and then we'll be free!

380
00:19:56,699 --> 00:19:59,199
Sorry to do it, Straw Hat,

381
00:19:59,199 --> 00:20:01,199
but we're taking control of this ship!

382
00:20:01,199 --> 00:20:03,199
We already broke out of prison,

383
00:20:03,199 --> 00:20:05,699
and we don't want dying to be the next thing we do!

384
00:20:05,699 --> 00:20:06,699
Surrender now!

385
00:20:06,699 --> 00:20:09,199
We've got Captain Buggy on our side.

386
00:20:09,199 --> 00:20:11,699
Tell him, Captain Buggy!

387
00:20:12,699 --> 00:20:16,699
Buggy, buggy, buggy, buggy, buggy, buggy, buggy!

388
00:20:16,699 --> 00:20:18,699
Only one way to handle this.

389
00:20:18,699 --> 00:20:19,699
Kill it.

390
00:20:22,199 --> 00:20:22,699
Good.

391
00:20:22,699 --> 00:20:23,699
I've got this!

392
00:20:23,699 --> 00:20:25,699
I really think I could do it!

393
00:20:26,199 --> 00:20:36,199
Buggy, buggy, buggy, buggy, buggy, buggy, buggy, buggy!

394
00:20:36,199 --> 00:20:37,699
Buggy, buggy, buggy, buggy!

395
00:20:37,699 --> 00:20:40,699
That's enough! Don't get too flashy!

396
00:20:40,699 --> 00:20:44,699
You guys are high on power and acting impulsively.

397
00:20:44,699 --> 00:20:47,699
No matter what, this ship's not stopping.

398
00:20:47,699 --> 00:20:49,699
We're headed straight for the heart of the war.

399
00:20:49,699 --> 00:20:52,699
And you guys are already on board, aren't you?

400
00:20:52,699 --> 00:20:54,699
Think about what that means for a second.

401
00:20:54,699 --> 00:21:00,699
In no time at all, we'll come face to face with a man standing with his foot on top of the world.

402
00:21:00,699 --> 00:21:04,699
Chances like this don't come around more than once in a lifetime.

403
00:21:04,699 --> 00:21:08,699
So listen, I want all of you to live out a dream with me.

404
00:21:08,699 --> 00:21:14,699
For today, I'll conquer Whitebeard and thus rule the world!

405
00:21:14,699 --> 00:21:17,699
Yeah! Captain Buggy!

406
00:21:23,699 --> 00:21:26,699
Captain Buggy!

407
00:21:26,699 --> 00:21:30,699
Thank you. The darkness of hell had beaten us down.

408
00:21:30,699 --> 00:21:35,699
You saved us! Gave us life! We almost lost the most important thing!

409
00:21:35,699 --> 00:21:37,699
Yes! Our dreams!

410
00:21:37,699 --> 00:21:39,699
You've got us dream again!

411
00:21:39,699 --> 00:21:41,699
I'll follow you anywhere, Captain Buggy!

412
00:21:41,699 --> 00:21:44,699
To hell with living a peaceful life!

413
00:21:46,699 --> 00:21:52,699
All right then! Let's win this war, you guys! To Navy HQ!

414
00:21:52,699 --> 00:21:55,699
War! Buggy! Buggy!

415
00:21:55,699 --> 00:21:57,699
So I guess the mutiny's over?

416
00:21:57,699 --> 00:22:00,699
Then he's not entirely useless, I suppose.

417
00:22:00,699 --> 00:22:03,699
You're gonna rule the world, Captain! I know it!

418
00:22:03,699 --> 00:22:05,699
I'm with you to the bitter end!

419
00:22:07,699 --> 00:22:09,699
That's right! You are!

420
00:22:11,699 --> 00:22:13,699
Let them have fun while they can.

421
00:22:14,699 --> 00:22:15,699
Huh?

422
00:22:15,699 --> 00:22:20,699
The ship transporting Port Castilles will arrive at Marineford shortly.

423
00:22:21,699 --> 00:22:22,699
Ah. Perfect.

424
00:22:29,699 --> 00:22:32,699
Right this way! Please board the ship!

425
00:22:32,699 --> 00:22:34,699
There's plenty of room, so don't worry!

426
00:22:34,699 --> 00:22:36,699
We'll get everyone on board!

427
00:22:40,699 --> 00:22:42,699
Prepare to receive the present arm!

428
00:22:45,699 --> 00:22:50,699
Let the ship out!

429
00:23:10,699 --> 00:23:14,699
Nami, traveling on the sky island of Wetheria, heads for the Grand Line.

430
00:23:14,699 --> 00:23:19,299
but the pace of the island's travel makes it unlikely that she'll ever reunite with her friends.

431
00:23:19,779 --> 00:23:23,879
Meanwhile, will Frankie be stuck as a tea-drinking gentleman forever?

432
00:23:24,619 --> 00:23:30,179
On the next One Piece, the Friends' Whereabouts, the Wetheria Report, and the Cyborg Animals,

433
00:23:30,639 --> 00:23:32,339
I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

